<section class="dx-section dx-replica-lifecycle" id="replica-lifecycle" aria-labelledby="replica-lifecycle-title">
    <header class="dx-section-heading">
        <div>
            <h2 id="replica-lifecycle-title">Winning the race is not enough</h2>
            <p>The task required two reads to run concurrently, while making sure each opened handle was closed correctly—even when its read lost the race.</p>
        </div>
    </header>
    <div class="dx-replica-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Two replicas each open a handle, read, and close with their own exit case. The first successful read wins; the other is canceled. The final result waits for cleanup of both replicas, and a cleanup exception remains a defect.">
        <div class="dx-replica-lanes">
            <div class="dx-replica-lane">
                <strong class="dx-replica-label">Replica A</strong>
                <span class="dx-replica-node">Open handle</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-node">Read</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-node dx-replica-release">Close (exit A)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="dx-replica-lane">
                <strong class="dx-replica-label">Replica B</strong>
                <span class="dx-replica-node">Open handle</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-node">Read</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="dx-replica-node dx-replica-release">Close (exit B)</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dx-replica-merge" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="dx-replica-end">
            <strong>First successful read wins</strong>
            <span>Cancel outstanding work · Await releases · Preserve cleanup defects</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="dx-replica-note">This diagram illustrates the behavior required by the <em>Replica read</em> evaluation task. A successful read does not excuse a losing replica from cleanup; the release receives that replica's own exit case.</p>
</section>
